{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1871 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "0c20ebc567ebc1db1a0203bf3a45088a23d668f131a4ca0e0dd9318b22da91b2" :edb/db-before-t 1870 :edb/db-after-t 1871 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535183 50 #inst "2026-10-13T02:32:29.132Z" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186087688 1038 #edb/ref 17592186478499 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186087688 1038 #edb/ref 17592186478500 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186087688 1038 #edb/ref 17592186478503 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186087688 1038 #edb/ref 17592186478508 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186087688 1038 #edb/ref 17592186478514 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186087688 1038 #edb/ref 17592186478516 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186087688 1038 #edb/ref 17592186478518 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186087688 1038 #edb/ref 17592186478519 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186087688 1038 #edb/ref 17592186478523 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186087688 1038 #edb/ref 17592186478526 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186087688 1040 #edb/ref 17592186478529 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478499 1068 #edb/ref 17592186478521 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478499 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478499 1071 "The lines $-21x - 12y = 108$ and $kx + 3y = 9$ are parallel. What is the value of $k$?$k =$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478499 1072 #uuid "04208a31-b2ae-567f-8896-e86342d6ce9d" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478499 1074 "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\n- To find the slope of the line $-21x - 12y = 108$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n-21x - 12y = 108\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -12y = 21x + 108\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y = - \\frac{7}{4}x - 9.\n$$\nIts slope is $- \\frac{7}{4}$.\n- To find the slope of the line $kx + 3y = 9$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\nkx + 3y = 9\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad 3y = -kx + 9\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y = -\\frac{k}{3}x + 3.\n$$\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $-\\dfrac{k}{3}$.\n\nSince the slopes of the two lines must be equal, we must have\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{k}{3}=- \\frac{7}{4}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $-3$ gives $k=\\frac{21}{4}$." 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478500 1068 #edb/ref 17592186478510 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478500 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478500 1071 "The lines $24x - 10y = 70$ and $kx + 4y = 12$ are parallel. What is the value of $k$?$k =$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478500 1072 #uuid "211d09f0-9544-5c60-a27a-1e3939da787d" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478500 1074 "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\n- To find the slope of the line $24x - 10y = 70$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n24x - 10y = 70\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -10y = -24x + 70\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y = \\frac{12}{5}x - 7.\n$$\nIts slope is $\\frac{12}{5}$.\n- To find the slope of the line $kx + 4y = 12$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\nkx + 4y = 12\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad 4y = -kx + 12\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y = -\\frac{k}{4}x + 3.\n$$\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $-\\dfrac{k}{4}$.\n\nSince the slopes of the two lines must be equal, we must have\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{k}{4}=\\frac{12}{5}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $-4$ gives $k=- \\frac{48}{5}$." 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478501 1080 "45" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478501 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478501 1083 #uuid "25484164-d56b-55cd-8788-5f282b6ba98e" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478502 1080 "10" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478502 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478502 1083 #uuid "27d765c0-4e75-5cf5-a4ad-5543fa562189" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478503 1068 #edb/ref 17592186478522 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478503 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478503 1071 "The lines $y = -7x + 0$ and $kx + 9y = -5$ are parallel. What is the value of $k$?$k =$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478503 1072 #uuid "2b6bd912-687a-541d-a6c5-b5a879018279" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478503 1074 "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\n- The line $y = -7x + 0$ is in slope-intercept form, and its slope is $-7$.\n- To find the slope of the line $kx + 9y = -5$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\nkx + 9y = -5\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad 9y = -kx - 5\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y = -\\frac{k}{9}x - \\frac{5}{9}.\n$$\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $-\\dfrac{k}{9}$.\n\nSince the slopes of the two lines must be equal, we must have\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{k}{9}=-7.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $-9$ gives $k=63$." 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478504 1080 "63" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478504 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478504 1083 #uuid "2bc4e6c7-209b-59fb-9cfe-0fd922736040" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478505 1075 #edb/ref 17592186478515 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478505 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478505 1077 "field-1" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478505 1078 #edb/ref 17592186478515 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478505 1079 #uuid "31b237ac-5c01-5409-9ef0-ff8e53ffc363" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478506 1075 #edb/ref 17592186478507 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478506 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478506 1077 "field-1" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478506 1078 #edb/ref 17592186478507 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478506 1079 #uuid "41021883-e0b3-57c5-b984-0654400ffc7f" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478507 1080 "\\frac{55}{4}" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478507 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478507 1083 #uuid "43e9a804-9f59-5019-9aa3-60392ef8ca28" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478508 1068 #edb/ref 17592186478512 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478508 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478508 1071 "The lines $x - 4y = 48$ and $kx - 4y = 12$ are parallel. What is the value of $k$?$k =$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478508 1072 #uuid "4dafc1fb-015c-56ff-bc14-52effb959f64" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478508 1074 "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\n- To find the slope of the line $x - 4y = 48$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\nx - 4y = 48\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -4y = -x + 48\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y = \\frac{1}{4}x - 12.\n$$\nIts slope is $\\frac{1}{4}$.\n- To find the slope of the line $kx - 4y = 12$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\nkx - 4y = 12\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -4y = -kx + 12\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y = \\frac{k}{4}x - 3.\n$$\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $\\dfrac{k}{4}$.\n\nSince the slopes of the two lines must be equal, we must have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{k}{4}=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $4$ gives $k=1$." 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478509 1075 #edb/ref 17592186478525 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478509 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478509 1077 "field-1" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478509 1078 #edb/ref 17592186478525 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478509 1079 #uuid "586b5446-0fe2-578a-878e-705eabf2af1b" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478510 1075 #edb/ref 17592186478524 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478510 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478510 1077 "field-1" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478510 1078 #edb/ref 17592186478524 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478510 1079 #uuid "5ce38150-54c5-55d5-a002-94896d315fb1" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478511 1080 "\\frac{49}{2}" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478511 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478511 1083 #uuid "5d995a2b-c1a5-5298-b2cc-a203c0911775" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478512 1075 #edb/ref 17592186478520 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478512 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478512 1077 "field-1" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478512 1078 #edb/ref 17592186478520 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478512 1079 #uuid "65aee0d1-2854-5e0c-93eb-7b4cd98f7548" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478513 1075 #edb/ref 17592186478501 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478513 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478513 1077 "field-1" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478513 1078 #edb/ref 17592186478501 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478513 1079 #uuid "7185e834-19ec-520c-872e-0e6e2b05f0ed" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478514 1068 #edb/ref 17592186478505 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478514 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478514 1071 "The lines $y = 3x + 6$ and $kx - 6y = -9$ are parallel. What is the value of $k$?$k =$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478514 1072 #uuid "72dbd957-6f59-540e-9ca7-2b36673b5f34" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478514 1074 "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\n- The line $y = 3x + 6$ is in slope-intercept form, and its slope is $3$.\n- To find the slope of the line $kx - 6y = -9$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\nkx - 6y = -9\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -6y = -kx - 9\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y = \\frac{k}{6}x + \\frac{3}{2}.\n$$\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $\\dfrac{k}{6}$.\n\nSince the slopes of the two lines must be equal, we must have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{k}{6}=3.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $6$ gives $k=18$." 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478515 1080 "18" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478515 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478515 1083 #uuid "7629e520-1dca-5eb9-886c-d80b56572f75" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478516 1068 #edb/ref 17592186478527 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478516 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478516 1071 "The lines $14x - 4y = -36$ and $kx - 7y = 0$ are parallel. What is the value of $k$?$k =$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478516 1072 #uuid "889f6a39-9b44-51a3-bbee-eb6f0f8b4ebb" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478516 1074 "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\n- To find the slope of the line $14x - 4y = -36$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n14x - 4y = -36\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -4y = -14x - 36\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y = \\frac{7}{2}x + 9.\n$$\nIts slope is $\\frac{7}{2}$.\n- To find the slope of the line $kx - 7y = 0$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\nkx - 7y = 0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -7y = -kx + 0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y = \\frac{k}{7}x + 0.\n$$\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $\\dfrac{k}{7}$.\n\nSince the slopes of the two lines must be equal, we must have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{k}{7}=\\frac{7}{2}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $7$ gives $k=\\frac{49}{2}$." 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478517 1075 #edb/ref 17592186478502 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478517 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478517 1077 "field-1" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478517 1078 #edb/ref 17592186478502 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478517 1079 #uuid "8c3a3128-a0b1-5e8f-9bdd-a028e9910c0f" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478518 1068 #edb/ref 17592186478513 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478518 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478518 1071 "The lines $y = 5x + 12$ and $kx - 9y = 12$ are parallel. What is the value of $k$?$k =$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478518 1072 #uuid "8f6b69ef-4822-5ea0-bc5a-d5e5650a7779" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478518 1074 "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\n- The line $y = 5x + 12$ is in slope-intercept form, and its slope is $5$.\n- To find the slope of the line $kx - 9y = 12$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\nkx - 9y = 12\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -9y = -kx + 12\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y = \\frac{k}{9}x - \\frac{4}{3}.\n$$\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $\\dfrac{k}{9}$.\n\nSince the slopes of the two lines must be equal, we must have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{k}{9}=5.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $9$ gives $k=45$." 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478519 1068 #edb/ref 17592186478506 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478519 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478519 1071 "The lines $-11x - 4y = 40$ and $kx + 5y = -11$ are parallel. What is the value of $k$?$k =$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478519 1072 #uuid "8fb31242-a4bd-58a8-a20e-be804320d787" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478519 1074 "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\n- To find the slope of the line $-11x - 4y = 40$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n-11x - 4y = 40\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -4y = 11x + 40\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y = - \\frac{11}{4}x - 10.\n$$\nIts slope is $- \\frac{11}{4}$.\n- To find the slope of the line $kx + 5y = -11$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\nkx + 5y = -11\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad 5y = -kx - 11\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y = -\\frac{k}{5}x - \\frac{11}{5}.\n$$\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $-\\dfrac{k}{5}$.\n\nSince the slopes of the two lines must be equal, we must have\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{k}{5}=- \\frac{11}{4}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $-5$ gives $k=\\frac{55}{4}$." 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478520 1080 "1" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478520 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478520 1083 #uuid "9ba1d3b5-6fee-59da-8756-7de1193bec63" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478521 1075 #edb/ref 17592186478528 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478521 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478521 1077 "field-1" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478521 1078 #edb/ref 17592186478528 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478521 1079 #uuid "9c379fc8-7257-5c47-9efa-e0f9d6f826a3" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478522 1075 #edb/ref 17592186478504 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478522 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478522 1077 "field-1" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478522 1078 #edb/ref 17592186478504 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478522 1079 #uuid "a02203b1-03c9-52de-9223-ab83694649cb" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478523 1068 #edb/ref 17592186478509 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478523 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478523 1071 "The lines $y = -12x + 6$ and $kx - 6y = -12$ are parallel. What is the value of $k$?$k =$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478523 1072 #uuid "a61ea21a-7ad8-549d-9c90-07bcff7c3c3a" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478523 1074 "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\n- The line $y = -12x + 6$ is in slope-intercept form, and its slope is $-12$.\n- To find the slope of the line $kx - 6y = -12$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\nkx - 6y = -12\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -6y = -kx - 12\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y = \\frac{k}{6}x + 2.\n$$\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $\\dfrac{k}{6}$.\n\nSince the slopes of the two lines must be equal, we must have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{k}{6}=-12.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $6$ gives $k=-72$." 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478524 1080 "- \\frac{48}{5}" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478524 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478524 1083 #uuid "b18772b2-e66f-5bbd-9b15-c5c090edd671" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478525 1080 "-72" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478525 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478525 1083 #uuid "c51d48f2-5613-5970-9e1b-d863e0b2dac3" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478526 1068 #edb/ref 17592186478517 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478526 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478526 1071 "The lines $y = 2x + 2$ and $kx - 5y = 9$ are parallel. What is the value of $k$?$k =$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478526 1072 #uuid "c691dbfe-adde-5dd9-8252-c74d417e06a8" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478526 1074 "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\n- The line $y = 2x + 2$ is in slope-intercept form, and its slope is $2$.\n- To find the slope of the line $kx - 5y = 9$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\nkx - 5y = 9\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -5y = -kx + 9\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y = \\frac{k}{5}x - \\frac{9}{5}.\n$$\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $\\dfrac{k}{5}$.\n\nSince the slopes of the two lines must be equal, we must have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{k}{5}=2.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $5$ gives $k=10$." 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478527 1075 #edb/ref 17592186478511 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478527 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478527 1077 "field-1" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478527 1078 #edb/ref 17592186478511 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478527 1079 #uuid "d4a978e5-f5fa-5ed7-8053-be55abcb58b3" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478528 1080 "\\frac{21}{4}" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478528 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478528 1083 #uuid "d64d33c3-8ae5-5650-9976-22a54c0377ee" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478529 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186087688.py" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true] [17592186478529 1169 #uuid "553548b2-9ae8-58f6-93d0-49b58d622766" 13194139535183 17592186045443 true]] :edb/tempids {"04208a31-b2ae-567f-8896-e86342d6ce9d" 17592186478499 "211d09f0-9544-5c60-a27a-1e3939da787d" 17592186478500 "25484164-d56b-55cd-8788-5f282b6ba98e" 17592186478501 "27d765c0-4e75-5cf5-a4ad-5543fa562189" 17592186478502 "2b6bd912-687a-541d-a6c5-b5a879018279" 17592186478503 "2bc4e6c7-209b-59fb-9cfe-0fd922736040" 17592186478504 "31b237ac-5c01-5409-9ef0-ff8e53ffc363" 17592186478505 "41021883-e0b3-57c5-b984